<!-- Statements come from the written assignment, solutions from the auto-   -->
<!-- graded version; each problem is a <problem> whose <solution> is printed -->
<!-- directly beneath it.  The auto-graded version is hw9-online.ptx.        -->
<!--                                                                        -->
<!-- HIDING THE SOLUTIONS.  Every <solution> here carries                    -->
<!--   component="hw9-solutions"                                            -->
<!-- so this assignment's solutions can be switched off from                 -->
<!-- publication/publication.ptx; see the comment in <source> there.         -->
<!-- Renumbered as Assignment 9; existing xml:ids keep exercise links and saved answers stable. -->
<section xml:id="sec-solutions-hw8" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Assignment 9</title>

    <p>
    Section: <xref ref="section-greens-theorem" text="title"/>.
    </p>

  <p>
    Work each problem yourself first; the full solution follows immediately
    below it. The auto-graded version of the same problems is
    <xref ref="sec-exercises-hw8-online" text="title"/>.
  </p>

  <problem xml:id="ex-hw8-staircase">
    <statement>
      <p>
      Compute the work done by the force field
      </p>

      <me>
      \mathbf{F} = \left\langle x^3 e^{x^2} + xe^x - y,\
      y^2 - e^y + x \right\rangle
      </me>

      <p>
      along the path <m>C</m>, which is shown in
      <xref ref="fig-hw8-staircase"/>. Assume that the object moves along
      the path from <m>(0,0)</m> to <m>(10,10)</m> and then to
      <m>(0,10)</m>.
      </p>
    </statement>
    <solution component="hw9-solutions">
      <p>
      Closing the path with the segment <m>C_3</m> down the
      <m>y</m>-axis gives a simple closed curve, and
      <m>\frac{\partial N}{\partial x} -
      \frac{\partial M}{\partial y} = 1-(-1) = 2</m>, so by Green's
      theorem, <xref ref="eq-green-tangential"/>, the closed loop
      integral is <m>2 \times 55 = 110</m>,
      where <m>55 = 50 + 10\left(\frac12\right)</m> is the enclosed
      area.
      </p>

      <p>
      On <m>C_3</m>, <m>x = 0</m> and <m>dx = 0</m>, so
      <m>\int_{C_3}\mathbf{F}\cdot d\mathbf{r}
      = \int_{10}^{0}\left(y^2-e^y\right) dy
      = -\frac{1000}{3}-1+e^{10}</m>. Therefore
      </p>

      <me>
      W = 110 + \frac{1000}{3} + 1 - e^{10}
      = \frac{1333}{3} - e^{10} \approx -21582.1 .
      </me>
    </solution>
  </problem>

